# Frontend UX Quality Bar

When creating or changing anything under `apps/web/`:

1. Read and follow the **Forms / Filters / Ant Design quality bar** in
   [`docs/technical/ui-requirements.md`](../../docs/technical/ui-requirements.md)
   (CHANGE-001 / US-042). Functional-but-bare screens are incomplete.
2. Every field: Azerbaijani label, placeholder, field-level validation
   (RHF + Zod + Ant `Form.Item`), correct input semantics.
3. Every list: usable FilterBar (search + status + domain filters), clear
   empty/loading/error/success, pagination with size changer, desktop table /
   mobile cards with all actions reachable.
4. Use Ant Design capabilities fully (`Select showSearch`, Modal confirm,
   Tag, Grid breakpoints, etc.). Do not invent a parallel design system.
5. Never expose enum keys, API field names, or raw backend messages.
6. Backend-generated codes (ADR-024) are read-only and never submitted.
7. If a required Azerbaijani business term is missing, stop per ADR-005 —
   except owner-approved routine labels for delivered enums (US-038 guidance).
